<Base title="About"><p class="eyebrow">About</p><h1>I'm Adeel.</h1>
<p class="lead">I enjoy building systems and growing the teams that operate them.</p>
<p>I'm based in Melbourne, Australia, with around 20 years of technology experience. My work has grown from hands-on infrastructure and cloud engineering into platform engineering, SRE, and engineering leadership.</p>
<p>I've helped operate high-volume transaction enrichment services, establish SRE practices, and grow a Platform Engineering capability from around one engineer to seven. I've stayed technically involved as the team's scope has grown.</p>
<div class="note"><p>My approach is to own reliability, deployment, cost, and security holistically.</p></div>
<p>That means looking at how an architectural decision affects the people deploying a service, the customer waiting for a response, and the engineer responding when something breaks.</p>
<h2>What I write about</h2><p>Production reliability, cloud cost, API performance, engineering leadership, and the lessons that emerge when assumptions meet operational reality.</p>
<p>I've been using AI as an enabler for SRE, reducing monitoring overhead through pragmatic use of AI agents with MCP connectivity to operational log sources. I share that work on <a href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/adeel-khan-1b42577/" rel="noreferrer">LinkedIn</a>.</p>
